Annotation Registers the bean when… Example <code>@ConditionalOnClass</code> / <code>@ConditionalOnMissingClass</code> a class is (not) on the classpath Redis support only if Lettuce is present <code>@ConditionalOnBean</code> / <code>@ConditionalOnMissingBean</code> a bean does (not) exist — the override mechanism Default <code>Clock</code> unless the app defines one <code>@ConditionalOnSingleCandidate</code> exactly one candidate (or a primary) exists Wire the only <code>DataSource</code> <code>@ConditionalOnProperty</code> a property has a value <code>grocery.tenancy.enabled=true</code> <code>@ConditionalOnBooleanProperty</code> a boolean property is true (newer Boot) — verify Feature toggle <code>@ConditionalOnResource</code> a resource exists A bundled model file <code>@ConditionalOnWebApplication</code> / <code>@ConditionalOnNotWebApplication</code> servlet/reactive/none Filters only in web apps <code>@ConditionalOnExpression</code> a SpEL expression is true Avoid — hard to debug <code>@ConditionalOnJava</code> a Java version range Virtual-thread-specific beans <code>@ConditionalOnCloudPlatform</code> running on Kubernetes, etc. Platform-specific defaults <code>@ConditionalOnThreading</code> platform or virtual threads active Executor choice <p>Conditions in practice (snippet)<pre><code>@Bean
@ConditionalOnMissingBean                                                   // the user's bean wins
@ConditionalOnProperty(prefix = "grocery.web", name = "enabled", havingValue = "true", matchIfMissing = true)
CorrelationIdFilter correlationIdFilter(GroceryWebProperties props) { ... }
</code></pre> Debug with <code>/actuator/conditions</code> or <code>--debug</code> (Chapter 41).</p>

