Annotation Checks Grocery example <code>@NotNull</code> Not null <code>@NotNull PaymentMethod method</code> <code>@NotBlank</code> String not null and not only whitespace <code>@NotBlank String sku</code> <code>@NotEmpty</code> String/collection/map not null and not empty <code>@NotEmpty List&lt;OrderLineRequest&gt; lines</code> <code>@Null</code> Must be null Server-assigned id on create <code>@Size(min, max)</code> Length or size <code>@Size(max = 200) String deliveryNote</code> <code>@Min</code> / <code>@Max</code> Integer bounds <code>@Min(1) @Max(20) int quantity</code> <code>@DecimalMin</code> / <code>@DecimalMax</code> Decimal bounds (as strings) <code>@DecimalMin("0.00") BigDecimal price</code> <code>@Positive</code> / <code>@PositiveOrZero</code> &gt; 0 / ≥ 0 <code>@PositiveOrZero BigDecimal deliveryFee</code> <code>@Negative</code> / <code>@NegativeOrZero</code> &lt; 0 / ≤ 0 Adjustments <code>@Digits(integer, fraction)</code> Digit counts <code>@Digits(integer = 7, fraction = 2) BigDecimal amount</code> <code>@Pattern(regexp)</code> Regex <code>@Pattern(regexp = "[A-Z0-9-]{3,40}") String sku</code> <code>@Email</code> Email syntax <code>@Email String email</code> <code>@Past</code> / <code>@PastOrPresent</code> Date in the past <code>@Past LocalDate dateOfBirth</code> <code>@Future</code> / <code>@FutureOrPresent</code> Date in the future <code>@FutureOrPresent LocalDate deliveryDate</code> <code>@AssertTrue</code> / <code>@AssertFalse</code> Boolean value; on methods for cross-field rules <code>@AssertTrue boolean isSlotWithinWindow()</code> DeliveryAddress.java<pre><code>public record DeliveryAddress(
        @NotBlank @Size(max = 120) String line1,
        @Size(max = 120) String line2,
        @NotBlank String city,
        @Pincode String pincode,
        @IndianMobile String contactMobile) {}
</code></pre>

ProductController.java<pre><code>package in.grocery.catalog.web;

import jakarta.validation.constraints.Max;
import jakarta.validation.constraints.Min;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Optional;
import org.springframework.validation.annotation.Validated;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/v1/stores/{pincode}/products")               // (1)!
@Validated                                                          // (2)!
class ProductController {

    private final ProductDelegate delegate;

    ProductController(ProductDelegate delegate) {
        this.delegate = delegate;
    }

    @GetMapping("/{sku}")
    ProductView bySku(@PathVariable @Pincode String pincode,         // (3)!
                      @PathVariable String sku) {
        return delegate.find(pincode, sku);
    }

    @GetMapping
    PageView&lt;ProductView&gt; search(
            @PathVariable @Pincode String pincode,
            @RequestParam(required = false) String q,                                   // (4)!
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "false") boolean includeOutOfStock,            // (5)!
            @RequestParam(name = "tag", required = false) List&lt;String&gt; tags,            // (6)!
            @RequestParam Optional&lt;String&gt; brand,                                       // (7)!
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") @Min(0) int page,
            @RequestParam(defaultValue = "20") @Min(1) @Max(100) int size) {            // (8)!
        return delegate.search(pincode, q, includeOutOfStock, tags, brand, page, size);
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>A placeholder at class level applies to every method in the controller.</li> <li>Needed for constraint annotations on individual parameters (Chapter 09).</li> <li>Names match the placeholders, so no <code>name</code> attribute is needed — as long as the code is compiled with <code>-parameters</code> (Boot's build plugins do this by default). If not, write <code>@PathVariable("sku")</code>.</li> <li><code>null</code> when absent.</li> <li><code>defaultValue</code> implies <code>required = false</code> and handles type conversion from the string <code>"false"</code>.</li> <li><code>?tag=organic&amp;tag=vegan</code> → <code>["organic", "vegan"]</code>. <code>name</code> maps a singular query name to a plural Java name.</li> <li><code>Optional&lt;T&gt;</code> is another way to say "not required".</li> <li>Always bound page sizes — an unbounded <code>size</code> is a denial-of-service vector (Chapter 20).</li> </ol> Request Result <code>GET /api/v1/stores/560102/products/ATTA-5KG</code> <code>bySku("560102", "ATTA-5KG")</code> <code>GET /api/v1/stores/560102/products?q=atta&amp;tag=organic&amp;tag=local</code> <code>search(..., q="atta", tags=[organic, local], page=0, size=20)</code> <code>GET /api/v1/stores/560102/products?size=500</code> <code>400</code> — <code>size</code> violates <code>@Max(100)</code> <code>GET /api/v1/stores/060102/products</code> <code>400</code> — invalid pincode <code>GET /api/v1/stores/560102/products?page=abc</code> <code>400</code> — <code>MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException</code>

