in/grocery/platform/json/GroceryJsonConfiguration.java (Boot 3.5)<pre><code>package in.grocery.platform.json;

import com.fasterxml.jackson.core.StreamReadConstraints;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.DeserializationFeature;
import com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.jackson.Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilderCustomizer;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;
import org.springframework.context.annotation.Configuration;
import org.springframework.http.converter.json.Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder;

@Configuration(proxyBeanMethods = false)
public class GroceryJsonConfiguration {

    @Bean
    Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilderCustomizer groceryJsonDefaults() {                   // (1)!
        return builder -&gt; builder
                .featuresToEnable(DeserializationFeature.READ_UNKNOWN_ENUM_VALUES_USING_DEFAULT_VALUE)
                .featuresToDisable(DeserializationFeature.FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES)
                .postConfigurer(mapper -&gt; mapper.getFactory().setStreamReadConstraints(
                        StreamReadConstraints.builder()
                                .maxNestingDepth(64)                               // (2)!
                                .maxStringLength(1_000_000)
                                .maxNumberLength(64)
                                .build()));
    }

    @Bean
    LogJson logJson(Jackson2ObjectMapperBuilder builder) {                         // (3)!
        return new LogJson(builder.build().registerModule(new SensitiveMaskingModule()));
    }

    /** Wrapper type on purpose — see note (3). */
    public static final class LogJson {
        private final ObjectMapper mapper;

        LogJson(ObjectMapper mapper) {
            this.mapper = mapper;
        }

        public String write(Object value) {
            try {
                return mapper.writeValueAsString(value);
            } catch (com.fasterxml.jackson.core.JsonProcessingException e) {
                return "{\"serializationError\":\"" + value.getClass().getSimpleName() + "\"}";   // never fail logging
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Adjusts Boot's builder — the primary mapper keeps all Boot defaults.</li> <li>Default nesting limit (1,000) is far beyond any legitimate grocery payload. <code>maxNumberLength</code> stops "a number with 100,000 digits" attacks on <code>BigDecimal</code> parsing.</li> <li>A second mapper for logs/audit with masking, built from Boot's (prototype-scoped) builder so it shares all defaults. It is wrapped in its own type on purpose: registering a second <code>ObjectMapper</code> bean would make Boot's <code>@ConditionalOnMissingBean(ObjectMapper.class)</code> primary mapper back off entirely. The API mapper stays untouched, so customers still see their own phone number in their profile response.</li> </ol> <p>Boot 4.x</p> <p>Use a <code>JsonMapperBuilderCustomizer</code> (verify name) and <code>JsonMapper.Builder</code> methods (<code>enable(...)</code>, <code>streamReadConstraints(...)</code> via the <code>JsonFactory</code> builder); derive the log mapper with <code>mapper.rebuild().addModule(new SensitiveMaskingModule()).build()</code> and keep it inside the <code>LogJson</code> wrapper for the same back-off reason. Jackson 3 mappers are immutable — "copy and modify" becomes "rebuild".</p>

