V31__order_customer_status_idx.sql<pre><code>set lock_timeout = '5s';
create index concurrently if not exists customer_order_status_idx
    on customer_order (status, placed_at)
    where status in ('PLACED', 'PAID', 'PACKED');
</code></pre> V31__order_customer_status_idx.sql.conf<pre><code>executeInTransaction=false
</code></pre> <p><code>CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY</code> can't run inside a transaction; the per-script config file tells Flyway to run it outside one.</p> <p>Failed concurrent index builds leave an INVALID index</p> <p>If it fails midway, PostgreSQL leaves an index marked <code>INVALID</code> that still slows writes. The retry must <code>DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF EXISTS ...</code> first, or check <code>pg_index.indisvalid</code>. Keep one concurrent index per migration so failures are easy to reason about.</p> <p>Verify</p> <p>Recent Flyway versions can auto-detect some non-transactional PostgreSQL statements; the explicit <code>.conf</code> file (or the <code>-- flyway:executeInTransaction=false</code> script directive, depending on version) is the unambiguous choice. Check your Flyway version's documentation.</p>

