    var results = redis.opsForGeo().radius("fleet:BLR",
            new Circle(new Point(lon, lat), new Distance(radiusKm, Metrics.KILOMETERS)), args);
    return results.getContent().stream().map(r -&gt; r.getContent().getName()).toList();
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Geo sets are sorted sets with geohash scores — location updates are cheap enough for a per-30-second ping from thousands of riders.</li> </ol>

in/grocery/platform/lock/RedisLock.java<pre><code>package in.grocery.platform.lock;

import java.time.Duration;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Optional;
import java.util.UUID;
import org.springframework.data.redis.core.StringRedisTemplate;
import org.springframework.data.redis.core.script.RedisScript;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

@Component
public class RedisLock {

    private static final RedisScript&lt;Long&gt; RELEASE = RedisScript.of(
            "if redis.call('get', KEYS[1]) == ARGV[1] then return redis.call('del', KEYS[1]) else return 0 end",
            Long.class);                                                          // (1)!

    private final StringRedisTemplate redis;

    public RedisLock(StringRedisTemplate redis) {
        this.redis = redis;
    }

    public Optional&lt;String&gt; tryAcquire(String name, Duration ttl) {
        String token = UUID.randomUUID().toString();
        Boolean acquired = redis.opsForValue().setIfAbsent("lock:" + name, token, ttl);   // (2)!
        return Boolean.TRUE.equals(acquired) ? Optional.of(token) : Optional.empty();
    }

    public void release(String name, String token) {
        redis.execute(RELEASE, List.of("lock:" + name), token);                   // (3)!
    }

    public &lt;T&gt; Optional&lt;T&gt; withLock(String name, Duration ttl, java.util.function.Supplier&lt;T&gt; work) {
        return tryAcquire(name, ttl).map(token -&gt; {
            try {
                return work.get();
            } finally {
                release(name, token);
            }
        });
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Compare-and-delete: only the owner releases. A plain <code>DEL</code> could delete a lock another pod acquired after ours expired.</li> <li><code>SET NX PX</code> — atomic acquire with expiry; the TTL is the safety valve if a pod dies.</li> <li>Still not a correctness guarantee: a long GC pause can let two pods believe they hold the lock. Use it for "don't run this nightly job twice", not for "don't double-charge a customer".</li> </ol> <p>ShedLock for scheduled jobs</p> <p>For <code>@Scheduled</code> deduplication across pods, the ShedLock library (backed by Redis or PostgreSQL) is a well-tested implementation of exactly this pattern (Chapter 25).</p>

