}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Named executor: notification work never competes with unrelated async work.</li> </ol> <p>Async and <code>@Transactional</code> don't share a transaction</p> <p>An <code>@Async</code> method runs on another thread with no transaction (and no security context). If it needs one, annotate it <code>@Transactional</code> — it will start its own. And remember: after-commit hooks (Chapter 03) are usually a better trigger than calling an async method inside a transaction.</p>

