in/grocery/tracking/client/EtaClient.java<pre><code>package in.grocery.tracking.client;

import java.time.Duration;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import org.springframework.web.reactive.function.client.WebClient;
import reactor.core.publisher.Mono;
import reactor.util.retry.Retry;

@Component
public class EtaClient {

    private final WebClient client;

    public EtaClient(WebClient.Builder builder) {                                 // (1)!
        this.client = builder.baseUrl("http://maps-service:8080").build();
    }

    public Mono&lt;EtaView&gt; eta(String from, String to) {
        return client.get()
                .uri("/api/eta?from={from}&amp;to={to}", from, to)
                .retrieve()
                .onStatus(status -&gt; status.is5xxServerError(),
                        response -&gt; Mono.error(DependencyException.unavailable("maps", null)))   // (2)!
                .bodyToMono(EtaView.class)
                .timeout(Duration.ofSeconds(1))                                                  // (3)!
                .retryWhen(Retry.backoff(2, Duration.ofMillis(100))                              // (4)!
                        .jitter(0.5)
                        .filter(DependencyException.class::isInstance))
                .onErrorResume(e -&gt; Mono.just(EtaView.approximate(from, to)));                   // (5)!
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Boot's builder brings codecs, metrics and tracing (Chapter 19's rule applies here too).</li> <li>Translate at the boundary.</li> <li>Timeouts are non-negotiable, reactive or not.</li> <li><code>retryWhen</code> with exponential backoff and jitter, filtered to transient failures only (Chapter 26).</li> <li>Degrade rather than fail — the fallback from Chapter 26, expressed as an operator.</li> </ol>

