in/grocery/tracking/service/PositionStream.java<pre><code>package in.grocery.tracking.service;

import java.time.Duration;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;
import reactor.core.publisher.Flux;

@Component
public class PositionStream {

    private final ReactiveRedisOperations&lt;String, RiderPosition&gt; redis;

    /** Live positions for one rider, safe for slow mobile clients. */
    public Flux&lt;RiderPosition&gt; forRider(String riderId) {
        return redis.listenToChannel("rider:" + riderId)                          // (1)!
                .map(message -&gt; message.getMessage())
                .onBackpressureDrop(dropped -&gt;                                     // (2)!
                        meters.counter("grocery.tracking.dropped").increment())
                .sample(Duration.ofSeconds(2))                                     // (3)!
                .timeout(Duration.ofMinutes(15))                                   // (4)!
                .doOnCancel(() -&gt; meters.counter("grocery.tracking.cancelled").increment());
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Reactive Redis pub/sub — a push source with no natural backpressure.</li> <li>Drop, don't buffer: for live positions, the newest value is the only valuable one, and buffering for a slow client is a memory leak with extra steps.</li> <li>Rate-limit per connection.</li> <li>Close abandoned connections; mobile clients disappear without closing sockets.</li> </ol> Feed type Strategy Live positions, prices, dashboards <code>onBackpressureDrop</code> / <code>onBackpressureLatest</code> + <code>sample</code> Paged data export <code>limitRate</code> — the consumer's demand controls the source Financial events (must not lose) Don't stream to the client; persist and let them poll/replay

