package grocery.pricing.v1;
option java_multiple_files = true;
option java_package = "in.grocery.pricing.grpc.v1";

service PricingService {
  rpc GetPrice(GetPriceRequest) returns (PriceResponse);                    // (1)!
  rpc GetPrices(GetPricesRequest) returns (stream PriceResponse);           // (2)!
}

message GetPriceRequest {
  string sku = 1;
  string pincode = 2;
}

message GetPricesRequest {
  repeated string skus = 1;
  string pincode = 2;
}

message PriceResponse {
  string sku = 1;
  string price_rupees = 2;        // decimal as string — never float        // (3)!
  string mrp_rupees = 3;
  reserved 4;                                                               // (4)!
  reserved "discount_percent";
  PriceSource source = 5;
}

enum PriceSource {
  PRICE_SOURCE_UNSPECIFIED = 0;                                             // (5)!
  PRICE_SOURCE_BASE = 1;
  PRICE_SOURCE_ZONE = 2;
  PRICE_SOURCE_PROMOTION = 3;
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Unary: request/response.</li> <li>Server-streaming: results flow as they're computed — useful for large SKU lists.</li> <li>Money as a string (or a dedicated <code>Money</code> message with units and nanos). <code>double</code> in a price field is a defect.</li> <li>A removed field's number and name are reserved forever so no future field reuses them.</li> <li>Proto3 enums must have a zero value named <code>_UNSPECIFIED</code> — it's what old clients see for new values.</li> </ol> in/grocery/pricing/grpc/PricingGrpcService.java<pre><code>package in.grocery.pricing.grpc;

import io.grpc.Status;
import io.grpc.stub.StreamObserver;
import in.grocery.pricing.grpc.v1.*;

@GrpcService                                                                  // (1)!
public class PricingGrpcService extends PricingServiceGrpc.PricingServiceImplBase {

    private final PricingService pricing;

    @Override
    public void getPrice(GetPriceRequest request, StreamObserver&lt;PriceResponse&gt; responseObserver) {
        try {
            var price = pricing.priceFor(request.getSku(), request.getPincode());
            if (price == null) {
                responseObserver.onError(Status.NOT_FOUND                     // (2)!
                        .withDescription("No price for " + request.getSku())
                        .asRuntimeException());
                return;
            }
            responseObserver.onNext(PriceResponse.newBuilder()
                    .setSku(price.sku())
                    .setPriceRupees(price.price().toPlainString())
                    .setMrpRupees(price.mrp().toPlainString())
                    .setSource(PriceSource.PRICE_SOURCE_ZONE)
                    .build());
            responseObserver.onCompleted();                                    // (3)!
        } catch (DependencyException e) {
            responseObserver.onError(Status.UNAVAILABLE.withCause(e).asRuntimeException());
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void getPrices(GetPricesRequest request, StreamObserver&lt;PriceResponse&gt; responseObserver) {
        if (request.getSkusCount() &gt; 500) {                                    // (4)!
            responseObserver.onError(Status.INVALID_ARGUMENT
                    .withDescription("At most 500 SKUs per request").asRuntimeException());
            return;
        }
        pricing.priceAll(request.getSkusList(), request.getPincode())
               .forEach(p -&gt; responseObserver.onNext(toResponse(p)));
        responseObserver.onCompleted();
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Annotation name depends on the starter (<code>@GrpcService</code> in both the community starter and Spring gRPC) — verify the import.</li> <li>Status codes are the error contract; map domain outcomes deliberately (<code>NOT_FOUND</code>, <code>INVALID_ARGUMENT</code>, <code>FAILED_PRECONDITION</code>, <code>RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED</code>, <code>UNAVAILABLE</code>).</li> <li>Exactly one <code>onCompleted()</code> or <code>onError()</code> per call — forgetting it leaks the stream until the deadline.</li> <li>Bound batch sizes, as with REST bulk endpoints.</li> </ol>

