in/grocery/ai/rag/PolicyIngestionService.java<pre><code>@Component
public class PolicyIngestionService {

    private final VectorStore vectorStore;

    public void ingest(Resource document, String source, String tenantId) {
        var reader = new TikaDocumentReader(document);                               // (1)!
        var splitter = new TokenTextSplitter(600, 120, 10, 5000, true);              // (2)!

        List&lt;Document&gt; chunks = splitter.apply(reader.get()).stream()
                .map(chunk -&gt; chunk.mutate()
                        .metadata(Map.of(
                                "source", source,
                                "tenantId", tenantId,                                 // (3)!
                                "updatedAt", Instant.now().toString(),
                                "url", publicUrlFor(source)))                         // (4)!
                        .build())
                .toList();

        vectorStore.delete(filterBySource(source));                                   // (5)!
        vectorStore.add(chunks);
    }
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Tika handles PDF, DOCX and HTML; PDF-specific readers preserve page structure better for long documents.</li> <li>~600-token chunks with overlap — a starting point to tune against evaluations, not a universal truth. Verify constructor parameters for your version.</li> <li>Tenant metadata is mandatory in a multi-tenant system (Chapter 38): retrieval filters on it, and a missing filter leaks one chain's policies into another's answers.</li> <li>A citation URL so answers can link to the source — the single most effective trust feature in a support assistant.</li> <li>Re-ingestion replaces the previous version of that source; otherwise stale chunks compete with current ones and the model cites last year's return policy.</li> </ol>

in/grocery/ai/rag/PolicyRetriever.java<pre><code>public List&lt;Document&gt; retrieve(String question, String tenantId) {
    return vectorStore.similaritySearch(SearchRequest.builder()
            .query(question)
            .topK(6)                                                                  // (1)!
            .similarityThreshold(0.5)                                                 // (2)!
            .filterExpression("tenantId == '%s'".formatted(tenantId))                 // (3)!
            .build());
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>More chunks means more context, more tokens and more noise. Tune with evaluations.</li> <li>A threshold, not just top-k: without it, an unrelated question still returns the six least-unrelated chunks, and the model dutifully answers from them.</li> <li>Tenant isolation at retrieval. Build the expression from a validated tenant id, never from user text.</li> </ol>

