scripts/dora.py (sketch)<pre><code># Inputs: deploy events (digest, service, time), commit timestamps, incident records
def lead_time(deploy, commits):
    return deploy.time - min(c.time for c in commits if c.sha in deploy.shas)     # (1)

def change_failure_rate(deploys, incidents):
    failed = {i.caused_by_deploy for i in incidents if i.caused_by_deploy}
    return len(failed) / max(len(deploys), 1)                                       # (2)

def time_to_restore(incidents):
    return median(i.resolved_at - i.detected_at for i in incidents)                 # (3)
</code></pre> <ol> <li>From the earliest commit in the release to production — measures the whole pipeline, including review and queue time.</li> <li>Requires incidents to record the deploy that caused them — a small discipline with a large payoff.</li> <li>Median, not mean; one long incident shouldn't hide steady improvement.</li> </ol> <p>Publish per service and team as trends, discussed in retrospectives. Never per engineer.</p>

